{{Main|2022 United States Senate special election in Oklahoma}}
Five-term incumbent Republican [[Jim Inhofe]] had been re-elected with 63% of the vote in 2020, and was not scheduled to be up for election again until 2026. However, Inhofe announced his intention to resign at the end of the [[117th United States Congress|117th Congress]]. A special election to fill his seat will take place in November 2022, concurrent with the other Senate elections.<ref name=Inhofe/> [[United States House of Representatives|U.S. representative]] [[Markwayne Mullin]] defeated [[Oklahoma House of Representatives|state House]] speaker [[T. W. Shannon]] in the runoff Republican primary election. Mullin and Shannon defeated Inhofe's [[Chief of Staff]] Luke Holland and others in the initial Republican primary election.<ref name=Holland>{{cite news |title=Luke Holland, Sen. Inhofe's chief of staff, announces candidacy for US Senate |url=https://www.koco.com/article/oklahoma-inhofe-resignation-announcement-luke-holland/39224241 |publisher=KOCO |date=February 25, 2022 |access-date=February 25, 2022}}</ref><ref name=Mullin>{{cite news |last1=Morris |first1=Callie |title=Rep. Markwayne Mullin announces run for Senate |url= https://ktul.com/news/local/markwayne-mullin-announces-run-for-us-senate |publisher=KTUL News |date=February 26, 2022 |access-date=February 26, 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=After eight years, Shannon ready for one more race |url=https://tulsaworld.com/news/state-and-regional/govt-and-politics/after-eight-years-shannon-ready-for-one-more-race/article_cd6fe3c0-a08a-11ec-a957-5b95c2684f38.html |access-date=March 10, 2022 |website=Tulsa World |date=March 10, 2022|author=Krehbiel, Randy}}</ref> Additionally, former U.S. representative [[Kendra Horn]] is the Democratic nominee, being her party's only candidate.<ref name=OK2022/><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.oklahoman.com/story/news/2022/03/15/former-lawmaker-kendra-horn-files-jim-inhofes-u-s-senate-seat-congress/7046491001/|title=Kendra Horn files for Jim Inhofe's Senate seat|last=Casteel|first=Chris|date=March 15, 2022|access-date=March 15, 2022|website=[[The Oklahoman]]}}</ref>
