One-term Republican [[Tim Scott]] was appointed in 2013 and won election to his first full term in [[2016 United States Senate election in South Carolina|2016]] with 60.6% of the vote. He said that while he is running for re-election in 2022, it would be his last time.<ref name="the hill august 9">{{cite news |author=Rachel Frazin |date=August 9, 2019 |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/456876-gop-sen-tim-scott-says-if-he-runs-in-2022-it-will-be-his-last-race |title=GOP Sen. Tim Scott says if he runs in 2022 it will be his last race |newspaper=The Hill}}</ref> In the Democratic primary, [[South Carolina House of Representatives|state representative]] [[Krystle Matthews]] defeated author and activist Catherine Fleming Bruce in a runoff.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Novelly |first1=Thomas |date=April 12, 2021 |title=Lowcountry Democratic lawmaker announces challenge to Republican Sen. Tim Scott in 2022 |url=https://www.postandcourier.com/politics/lowcountry-democratic-lawmaker-announces-challenge-to-republican-sen-tim-scott-in-2022/article_33132282-9baf-11eb-940e-972d7bbee7a2.html |access-date=April 13, 2021 |website=Post and Courier |language=en}}</ref> Angela Geter, chairwoman of the Spartanburg County Democratic Party, also ran in the primary.<ref>{{cite web|last=Conradis|first=Brandon|date=2022-01-21|title=These Senate seats are up for election in 2022|url=https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/590812-these-senate-seats-are-up-for-election-in-2022|access-date=2022-01-29|website=The Hill|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|agency=Associated Press|date=April 12, 2021|title=Democrat says registration key to ousting SC's Tim Scott|url=https://www.dailyherald.com/article/20210412/news/304129956|access-date=April 12, 2021|website=Daily Herald|author=Kinnard, Meg}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Montgomery |first1=Bob |title=Spartanburg's Dem chair announces bid for U.S. Senator Tim Scott's seat |url=https://www.goupstate.com/story/news/local/2021/05/05/spartanburg-democratic-chair-angela-geter-bid-u-s-senate-tim-scott-seat/4878871001/ |website=GoUpstate |access-date=May 6, 2021|date=May 6, 2021}}</ref>

